=== BD l.429
- **Existence:** a body ends from a fact (BD2): `starved` (supplies at zero for DRAFT 3 weeks — gang, beast), `scattered` (cohesion below 0.1, or a fight lost at `thin`, or its own `scatter` choice — gang), `dissolved` (a conclave received into a town by `attemptEntry`, or one whose court turned `permitted` while it stood in that town — it is that town's row again), `merged` (absorbed in a meeting), `raised` (the DM's promotion, BD16), `disbanded` (the DM's end). Each end leaves its `ended` row (the ring) and a Herald line; its pairs drop; its site falls EMPTY (ST's `abandoned`, through ST's writer); its standings stop composing (no write: §7.3 reads the live records).
=== BD l.473
- **The hearing `body_stance` (§12):** minted the week the court's FORK would change the standing word — its inputs the default above, the body's deeds in the court's land (a raid, a sheltering, a fight against a gang), a `supplicate` (a conclave's petition for leave or a shrine), a `bribe`, the liege's ORDER to hunt (PL's `huntOrderOf`, the precedence's call line — an INPUT LINE on this fork, PL §4.8 (2)), a war's need for irregulars (§9.8); and, from round 4 [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — L-BD 29 · 30 · 39 · 23b · 43 · 46 · 48 · ST's route (d)]: the ALMS a far god's flock drew this season, weighted by the patron creed's share and legitimacy (§6.6); a flock's REFUSAL of a demanded sale (ST's `site_sale` `refused` moves the fork ONE STEP toward `curbed`); the court's own LESSON (HB's court row, §4.4 (a): a court that has curbed flocks drifts toward curbing the next); the LIEGE'S FAITH (a member curbing or outlawing a flock of its liege's own creed pays the liege's resentment and a step of the crown's protection, §10.2 (b′) — the mirror counterforce); the COMMONS' stance (a court hesitates to hunt a body its own people SUPPORT, §7.6); a LEAK that exposes a sponsor's hand in the body (the host court's fork is pressed to `hunted`, §10.4); and an OUTRAGE — a body that struck an envoy on public mission or a contracted caravan of this court (§9.5) pushes the court's fork to `hunted` and its bounty fork open (§9.9). A SEIZURE of a flock's site instead of a sale is the court's own choice: its fork turns `outlawed` (the flock hostile from that week, item 15) and ST's clearing follows (ST §6.1 step 6). DEFAULT: the fork's new word. The DM may leave, tilt (a bias on the fork's `net`, ±0.1 / ±0.3, DRAFT) or decide any word of the subject's line. After the court's act the CONCLAVE CHOOSES (`hide` · `defy` · `move`, §4.2) — the owner's "lie low · defy · move".
=== BD l.516
THE BODIES REGISTER ONE ROW, `bodyPresenceFeeder(T)`, into MN §3.3's `roadCountry(T)` part of `spatial/presenceComposer.js :: presenceTerms` (A.3's shared car — "a later feeder — THE BODIES' road-country row … joins by the same door and nowhere else"), gated by `bodyEffectsEnabled`, read where the canon marker is present. Per country T: the MAX over the bodies whose `where` touches T this week (a body on the stretch `a|b` touches both; a body on a trail touches nothing unless it SORTIED this week; a body at a site attached `at_hand` to T touches T) of `PRESENCE_BY_MIGHT[might] × ACT_FACTOR[act]` — DRAFT `thin` 0.35 · `modest` 0.50 · `capable` 0.60 · `strong`/`formidable` 0.70; `ACT_FACTOR` raiding this week 1.0, based in the country 0.8, passing 0.5; a beast in WINTER × 1.2 — so a `capable` raiding body latches a calm, unwatched country on its own (0.60 > 0.55), a `modest` one latches it only with the country's own crime, a `thin` one only sustains a country already embattled (above 0.30). The row sits on MN's SUPPRESSIBLE side: a held keep and the riders take up to the shared cap `σ(T) = min(0.25, siteSuppression(T) + patrolSubtraction(T))` off it (A.1) — a watched, kept country where a `capable` gang raids reads 0.35 and never latches. The composer caps every row once at `PRESENCE_TERM_CAP` and takes the MAX over feeders, so a body at an ST den does not count twice: where an untied site's holder IS a body, ST's `sitePresenceFeeder` reads zero for that site and the body's row carries it (one term per thing — CARRIED in ST at round 4a: zero where `bodyEffectsEnabled` is lit, the record's might where it is dark, BD §15). [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — ST's route (b): the PER-BODY part of the row is exposed by name, `bodyPresenceTermOf(worldState, bodyId, settlementId) → p01` (`PRESENCE_BY_MIGHT[might] × ACT_FACTOR[act]` for that one body at that town, before the MAX and the suppression), so ST's `denPressOf` reads the one term the composer carries for a body holder and never recomputes it.]
=== BD l.557
- **A PEACEABLE FLOCK AND A SITE (the owner, ~19:4x: "non hostile conclaves can occupy a site or attack one hosted by hostile forces. In such cases, they may not be pursued by settlement but may be forced to give it up in exchange for resources") [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — L-BD 30 · ST's route (d)]:** a flock no court in its reach holds `outlawed` may TAKE an EMPTY site (ST's `site_taken`, the flock the arriver; it holds as `faith`, §2.1) or CLEAR a site a HOSTILE body holds (ST's `site_cleared`, the flock the clearer — a good god's militants on a gang's den, §4.2), and the town does NOT pursue it for either (pursuit is by stance, §7.1; PR §5.5). "Forced to give it up in exchange for resources" is ST's OWN kind `site_sale` (ST §6.1 step 6b, §8; minted by ST in round 4a — CLIMAX, WHERE `site`, verdicts `sold · refused`): an attached court that holds the flock's creed `permitted` or `curbed` DEMANDS the site against a price; the FLOCK answers by its god's recorded axes (ST's `saleFork`, no randomness: lawful yields at a fair price, chaotic may refuse, good yields where the people are served); `sold` pays the price INTO the flock's supplies through BD's one writer (`bodySupply01` + DRAFT 0.5, UNMEASURED; the court's coin is the W-COIN slot) and the flock leaves the site (ST's `conveyed`); `refused` moves the court's `body_stance` fork ONE STEP toward `curbed` (§7.1 — the counterforce; the court's next act is its own hearing). A SEIZURE instead of a sale is the court's choice: it turns the flock `outlawed` (hostile, item 15) and clears it (ST §6.1 step 6). No new verb.
=== BD l.1060
| A2 | any body PRESENT in a country (based · passing · raiding; a beast in winter) (§8.2) | the EMBATTLED GAUGE (the ledger, not a stressor) → the landed road losses, routing, migration deaths, supply, the T3 gauntlet | ONE row of the shared presence composer's `roadCountry`, capped, MAX-composed, suppressible | ⚠ DECLARED TWO-CHANNEL: a raiding body reaches the gauge directly (A2) AND through A1's stressor (its `conflict`/`crime` pressure → the kernel's security and crime terms). Both are bounded (`PRESENCE_TERM_CAP`; `rampThreat`'s `SECURITY_MAX_RELIEF 0.25` and `CRIME_FLOOR`), the second is the town's CRISIS (fear, the militia's burden) and the first the road's PRESENCE — two facts the landed ramp already keeps apart; BD-2's re-feed measurement (OD-BD-2) reports both arms' share, and the seams skeptic attacks it here |
